    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Font Pré is at 17 avenue de l'Elisa, in Toulon. It welcomes pets and small exotic pets for medicine and surgery consultations, and is equipped with X-ray and ultrasound, for your dog's care during your stay in the Var.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The phone number, 04 94 14 31 30, and the hours are those of the official website cliniqueveterinairefontpre.com: Monday-Friday 8:30am-12pm and 2:30pm-7pm, Saturday 8:30am-12pm and 2:30pm-5pm, closed on Sunday. The site writes "emergencies during opening hours" next to the number, and does not mention a night on-call service. To book an appointment, it asks you to phone.</p>
      <p>Team shown on the site: Dr Laurent Magne (Alfort veterinary school) and two veterinary nursing assistants. Languages spoken: French, English, German and Italian, a plus if you are travelling with your dog from abroad. As for species, the site lists in particular dogs, cats, rabbits, the ferret, small rodents and birds, as well as farm animals. Pet insurance is accepted, and the site offers an e-health record (customer account) to view the animal's medical information, as well as an online shop. Outside opening hours, the site names no on-call clinic: for a night or Sunday emergency, look for a nearby 24/7 clinic (see the "Nearest 24/7 emergency vets" box on this page, when it appears).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save the clinic's official website in your bookmarks as soon as you arrive in Toulon — it can come in handy if something unexpected comes up.</div>

